-- Canonical Nigerian geography reference data, for databases where V14 sits
-- below the Flyway baseline and so never ran (staging and prod both).
--
-- V25 deliberately deferred this on the grounds that address geo is nullable and
-- does not block booking. That was true of booking, but wrong for the admin
-- portal: Regions and Zones are built by picking states and LGAs, so with these
-- tables empty every one of those pickers is an empty list and the whole
-- geographic side of Permission Architecture V2 is unusable. Seeding it now.
--
-- 37 states (36 + FCT), 774 LGAs, Nigeria's 6 geopolitical zones as regions, and
-- the state->region memberships. Full provenance is documented in the header of
-- V14__seed_states_lgas_regions.sql; the rows below are copied from it verbatim,
-- rewritten only to be idempotent.
--
-- Idempotency uses WHERE NOT EXISTS / ON CONFLICT rather than assuming a unique
-- constraint name: these tables were created by ddl-auto, so their index names
-- are Hibernate-generated and differ from what V13 would have produced. Re-running
-- is a no-op, and a database that already has V14's rows is left untouched.




-- LGA name aliases (from V16). Google's administrative_area_level_2 does not
-- always spell an LGA the way the official register does; these are the two
-- misses measured against the live Geocoding API, plus the everyday short form
-- of the FCT's Municipal Area Council. Without them those addresses fall to the
-- unresolved queue. Keyed on the id so a re-run is a no-op.
SELECT 'alias-fct-amac', l.id, l.state_id, 'abujamunicipalareacouncil', 'SEED'
FROM lgas l JOIN states s ON s.id = l.state_id
WHERE s.normalized_name = 'federalcapitalterritory'
  AND l.normalized_name = 'municipalareacouncil'
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

SELECT 'alias-kano-nassarawa', l.id, l.state_id, 'nassarawa', 'SEED'
FROM lgas l JOIN states s ON s.id = l.state_id
WHERE s.normalized_name = 'kano'
  AND l.normalized_name = 'nasarawa'
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

SELECT 'alias-fct-amac-short', l.id, l.state_id, 'amac', 'SEED'
FROM lgas l JOIN states s ON s.id = l.state_id
WHERE s.normalized_name = 'federalcapitalterritory'
  AND l.normalized_name = 'municipalareacouncil'
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
